ra's general takes Udayagiri and Chandragiri.","cp":"vijayanagara-empire","cpn":"Vijayanagara Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kapilendra_Deva","c":2},{"y":1472,"t":"loss","x":"1472: the Bahmanis take Rajahmundry and Kondavidu in the civil war.","cp":"bahmani-sultanate","cpn":"Bahmani Sultanate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purushottama_Deva","c":1},{"y":1472,"t":"loss","x":"1472: Saluva Narasimha takes Udayagiri and Chandragiri.","cp":"vijayanagara-empire","cpn":"Vijayanagara Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purushottama_Deva","c":1},{"y":1476,"t":"gain","x":"1476: Udayagiri and Chandragiri return.","cp":"vijayanagara-empire","cpn":"Vijayanagara Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purushottama_Deva","c":1},{"y":1500,"t":"gain","x":"1500: Prataparudra reaches the Krishna.","m":11,"cp":"bahmani-sultanate","cpn":"Bahmani Sultanate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prataparudra_Deva","c":2},{"y":1512,"t":"contest_start","x":"1512: Vijayanagara besieges Udayagiri.","cp":"vijayanagara-empire","cpn":"Vijayanagara Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krishnadevaraya","c":3},{"y":1514,"t":"contest_end","x":"1514: Udayagiri surrenders.","cp":"vijayanagara-empire","cpn":"Vijayanagara Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prataparudra_Deva","c":3},{"y":1514,"t":"loss","x":"1514: Udayagiri is lost to Vijayanagara.","cp":"vijayanagara-empire","cpn":"Vijayanagara Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prataparudra_Deva","c":2},{"y":1516,"t":"loss","x":"1516: Krishnadevaraya takes Kondavidu.","cp":"vijayanagara-empire","cpn":"Vijayanagara Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kondavidu_Fort","c":3},{"y":1531,"t":"loss","x":"1531: Quli Qutb Shah takes Kondapalli.","m":3,"cp":"golconda-sultanate","cpn":"Golconda Sultanate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prataparudra_Deva","c":2},{"y":1541,"t":"dissolve","x":"1541: the Gajapati line ends in Odisha.","cp":"bhoi-dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gajapati_Kingdom","c":2}],"wars":[{"name":"Gajapati-Bengal war","from":1447,"to":1450,"outcome":"The Gajapatis took the territory west of the Ganga in 1447; a Puri inscription of 1450 narrates the conquest of Gauda, which is not drawn.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kapilendra_Deva"},{"name":"Kapilendra's conquest of the Reddi kingdoms","from":1446,"to":1454,"outcome":"Rajahmundry was Kapilendra's before 1448 and Kondavidu after August 1453; by 1454 he was master of both.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kapilendra_Deva"},{"name":"Gajapati-Bahmani wars","from":1458,"to":1461,"outcome":"A battle at Devarakonda in 1458 and a 'significant military campaign' in 1461; no territory is dated.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kapilendra_Deva"},{"name":"Gajapati civil war","from":1467,"to":1476,"outcome":"Purushottama lost more than half of his father's empire to Hamvira and the Bahmanis; Udayagiri and Chandragiri came back after the Kanchi expedition.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purushottama_Deva"},{"name":"Vijayanagara-Gajapati war","from":1512,"to":1516,"outcome":"Udayagiri surrendered in 1514, Kondavidu fell in 1516 and the lands north of the Krishna were returned, making the river the frontier.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krishnadevaraya"},{"name":"Qutb Shahi invasion of the Gajapati south","from":1531,"to":1531,"outcome":"Quli Qutb Shah took Kondapalli on 20 March 1531 with many forts of the south.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prataparudra_Deva"}],"certainty":[{"from":1434,"to":1541,"level":"soft","note":"No treaty line is named on any page opened; the Krishna as the boundary with Vijayanagara after the war of 1512-1516 is the nearest to a fixed line and is undated."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gajapati_Kingdom","title":"Gajapati Kingdom"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kapilendra_Deva","title":"Kapilendra Deva"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purushottama_Deva","title":"Purushottama Deva"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.o